// Example 3: The Merchant
// Demonstrating dialogue and character interaction

=== start ===

You enter a dusty old shop filled with strange artifacts.

An old merchant looks up from behind the counter.

"Welcome, traveler! Looking for something special?"

* [Ask about the shop] -> about_shop
* [Ask what they sell] -> what_sell
* [Leave immediately] -> leave

=== about_shop ===

"Ah, this shop has been in my family for generations," the merchant says.

"We deal in... unusual items. Things you won't find anywhere else."

They lean in conspiratorially.

"Some say cursed. I say... misunderstood."

* [Sounds interesting. What do you have?] -> what_sell
* [Cursed? No thanks!] -> leave_scared

=== what_sell ===

The merchant gestures around the shop.

"I have potions, scrolls, enchanted weapons... even a few odds and ends whose purpose I'm not quite sure of."

"What catches your eye?"

* [Ask about the glowing amulet] -> amulet
* [Ask about the ancient book] -> book
* [Actually, I should go] -> leave

=== amulet ===

"Ah, the Amulet of True Sight," the merchant says, carefully taking it from the shelf.

"They say it lets you see through illusions. Very rare. Very expensive."

"It's yours for... hmm... how about 500 gold pieces?"

* [That's too much!] -> haggle
* [I'll take it!] -> buy_amulet
* [Let me look at something else] -> what_sell

=== book ===

The merchant carefully opens the leather-bound tome.

"The Lost Grimoire of Shadows. Very dangerous. Very powerful."

"Are you sure you can handle such knowledge?"

* [Yes, I'll take it] -> buy_book
* [On second thought...] -> what_sell

=== haggle ===

"Too much?" The merchant chuckles. "Perhaps you're right."

"Tell you what... 350 gold. Final offer."

* [Deal!] -> buy_amulet
* [Still too expensive] -> what_sell

=== buy_amulet ===

You purchase the Amulet of True Sight.

As you put it on, the shop seems to shimmer...

The merchant winks at you.

"Use it wisely, friend."

-> shop_end

=== buy_book ===

You purchase the ancient grimoire.

The moment it's in your hands, you feel its power.

The merchant nods solemnly.

"May you use that knowledge well."

-> shop_end

=== leave ===

"Come back anytime, traveler! I always have new stock!"

-> shop_end

=== leave_scared ===

You quickly back out of the shop.

Maybe you're not ready for this kind of adventure yet.

-> shop_end

=== shop_end ===

THE END

Thanks for visiting the merchant's shop!
